@* A sign-in card that works with scripting off and swaps in place with Unpoly.

   Two things here are load-bearing and get forgotten:

   up-target="body" — signing in crosses the auth boundary, so the whole shell has to be
   replaced. Target a fragment and the new page arrives wearing the signed-out chrome.

   up-fail-target on the FORM, not on a div inside it — [up-disable] disables every field while
   the request is out, including the antiforgery token. If the failure render does not replace
   the form itself, those fields stay disabled, are not serialized, and the next submit is a 400. *@

<div class="flex min-h-[60vh] items-center justify-center">
    <Card Class="w-full max-w-sm">
        <CardHeader>
            <CardTitle>Sign in</CardTitle>
            <CardDescription>Use the email you registered with.</CardDescription>
        </CardHeader>

        <form method="post" class="login-form" up-target="body" up-fail-target=".login-form">
            <CardContent Class="space-y-4">
                <FormField For="login-email" Label="Email">
                    <Input id="login-email" name="email" type="email" required
                           autocomplete="username" placeholder="you@example.com" />
                </FormField>

                <FormField For="login-password" Label="Password">
                    <Input id="login-password" name="password" type="password" required
                           autocomplete="current-password" />
                </FormField>

                <Label Class="flex w-fit cursor-pointer items-center gap-2.5 text-sm">
                    <Checkbox name="remember" value="true" />
                    <span>Keep me signed in</span>
                </Label>
            </CardContent>

            <CardFooter Class="mt-6 flex-col gap-3">
                <Button Class="w-full" up-disable>Sign in</Button>
                <a href="/reset" class="text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground">
                    Forgotten your password?
                </a>
            </CardFooter>
        </form>
    </Card>
</div>
